Good catch! Readability is absolutely critical for error messages. If the background is too dark or too intensely red, it makes the text completely unreadable.
We will style the Error Alert exactly like we styled the Success banner: a very light, soft background with highly visible dark text and a clean border.
Here is the exact block to replace in **JournalBulkUpload.js**.
**Find this block (around line 465):**
```javascript
          {resultStatus === "ERROR" && (
            <Alert
              severity="error"
              sx={{ mt: 3, mx: "auto", maxWidth: "100%",  color: "black", "& .MuiAlert-icon": { color: "error.main" } }}
            >
              {resultMsg} — {downloadMsg}
            </Alert>
          )}

```
**Replace it entirely with this:**
```javascript
          {resultStatus === "ERROR" && (
            <Alert
              severity="error"
              sx={{ 
                mt: 3, 
                mx: "auto", 
                maxWidth: "100%", 
                backgroundColor: "#fff5f5",  // Very light, soft red background
                color: "#c62828",            // Dark, highly visible red text
                border: "1px solid #ffcdd2", // Soft red border for structure
                "& .MuiAlert-icon": { color: "#d32f2f" },
                "& .MuiAlert-message": { width: "100%" }
              }}
            >
              <Typography variant="body1" fontWeight="500">
                {resultMsg} {downloadMsg ? `— ${downloadMsg}` : ""}
              </Typography>
            </Alert>
          )}

```
This will give you a beautiful, professional error banner where the text pops out perfectly!
